course: dictionary
lesson: 8424
title: Words with more than one meaning
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one the writer means. The word rut is a good example. «In the autumn rut, red deer stags roar, walk side by side and sometimes lock antlers.» Here rut is a time of year in nature, not a track in the mud.
explain: Look at the words around the tricky word. Autumn, stags and antlers are about animals, so rut must be about animals too. A deep line in mud would not fit with stags and antlers.
explain: Rut can also be a deep line in soft ground, made by wheels. It can be an idiom too: "stuck in a rut" means your life feels boring and the same every day. When you meet a word with more than one meaning, try each meaning in the sentence and see which one makes sense.
fact: Context means the words and sentences around a word.
fact: «Rut» means a deep line in soft ground made by wheels.
fact: «Stuck in a rut» means your life or habits are boring and hard to change.
fact: In nature, «rut» is the season when male deer and some other animals fight and look for mates.
fact: Many words have more than one meaning, so always check the context before you decide.
exercise: «In the autumn rut, red deer stags roar, walk side by side and sometimes lock antlers.» What is the rut here? | A boring habit | A deep line in the mud | *The season when male deer fight and look for mates | A type of tree
exercise: Dad says, «I'm stuck in a rut at work.» What does he mean? | He is stuck in a deep line in the mud | *His job feels boring and the same every day | He has hurt his back | He is lost on a long walk
exercise: Find and copy the word that means a deep line made by wheels: «The tractor left deep ruts in the wet field.» | *ruts | wheels | field | tractor
test: What does the phrase «get out of a rut» mean? | To jump over a deep line | To dig a hole in the ground | *To change a boring habit | To run very fast
test: Which animals does the word rut describe in the nature sentence? | Cats and dogs | Ducks and geese | Rabbits and foxes | *Red deer stags
exam: Which sentence uses rut to mean a deep line in soft ground? | *The tractor left ruts across the muddy field | The stags are in the rut every autumn | He has been stuck in a rut for years | The rut is a very dull way to live
